cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GATC — Gene Assembly & Toolkit for Cloning"
message: "If you use GATC in work you publish, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Qiu
    given-names: Shui
    alias: ArchitektSpeer
repository-code: "https://github.com/ArchitektSpeer/GATC"
url: "https://github.com/ArchitektSpeer/GATC"
abstract: >-
  An open-source, offline-first molecular biology workbench: plasmid maps, sequence editing,
  restriction and cloning simulation, primer design, Sanger and multiple sequence alignment and
  virtual gels. It reads and writes the SnapGene .dna format alongside GenBank, FASTA, EMBL and
  other common formats. Every computation is cross-checked against an independent
  implementation (Biopython, REBASE, primer3 and pydna).
keywords:
  - molecular-biology
  - molecular-cloning
  - plasmid
  - sequence-analysis
  - restriction-enzyme
  - primer-design
  - bioinformatics
  - snapgene
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-27"
